 "lineas": [
  {
   "texto": "Your town sits on flat land, right next to a big river.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Every spring the river rises, and floods your streets.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you pile up a long wall of earth along the bank. That's a dike.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "The Dutch have built dikes for about a thousand years.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Today, about a quarter of their country sits below sea level.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "But behind the dike, the rain has nowhere to go, and your fields turn into a swamp.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So, like the Dutch, you pump it up and over into the river. First with windmills, now with electric pumps.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Then a big flood pushes the river higher than ever.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Water seeps under the dike, through a hidden layer of sand.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "On the town side, little fountains of sand start bubbling out of the ground.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Each one is the dike's foundation washing away. It can collapse from below.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "So you drive a steel wall deep into the ground, right through the sand.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Now the water has no path under the dike.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "And you give it a core of tight clay and a skin of grass, so it can't wash out.",
   "pausa": 0.3
  },
  {
   "texto": "Congratulations! You just kept a whole country dry. What should we build next?",
   "pausa": 0.3
  }
 ],
